/-!
# Spreading out line bundles, and changing an algebraically closed ground field

This file proves two results used to move fourfold minimal model programs between fibres and
between ground fields.

**Line bundles on very general fibres.** Let `(Y, Θ, T, π)` be a local setting and `T° ⊆ T` a
`π`-adapted open, with family `𝓕 = Ỹ ×_Y T° ⟶ T°` and resolution local system
`𝒲 = (R²π_* ℚ_Ỹ)|_{T°}`. There is a countable set `Ω` of proper closed subsets of `T°` such that
for every complex point `t ∈ T° ∖ ⋃ Ω` and every line bundle `𝓛` on the fibre `F_t` there are a
dense open `T¹ ⊆ T°`, a connected finite étale cover `φ : T' ⟶ T¹`, a line bundle `𝓛'` on
`𝓕 ×_{T°} T'`, a complex point `t'` of `T'` over `t₁ = φ(t')` and a path `γ` in `T°(ℂ)` from `t`
to `t₁` along which parallel transport in `𝒲` carries `c₁(𝓛)` to `c₁(𝓛'|_{F_{t₁} × {t'}})`.

The line bundles on the fibres are parametrized by countably many `T°`-schemes of finite type
`M α` with universal bundles `𝓤 α`. `Ω` consists of the closures of the images of the
irreducible components of the `M α` which do not dominate `T°`. For `t ∉ ⋃ Ω`, `𝓛` is the
restriction of `𝓤 α` at a complex point `μ` of `M α` lying on a dominating component. The
closure `W` of the generic point of that component in an affine chart is an integral affine
`T°`-scheme through `μ` dominating `T°`; a closed point of its generic fibre spreads out to a
finite étale cover `T' ⟶ T¹` with a `T°`-morphism `T' ⟶ W`, and `𝓛'` is the pullback of `𝓤 α`.
The Chern classes of the restrictions of `𝓤 α` to the fibres over `W(ℂ)` are realized by germs
forming a family locally given by sections of `𝒲` (by the fibre comparison for proper maps), and
a path in the path connected space `W(ℂ)` projects to `γ`.

**Change of ground field.** Let `k₀ ⊆ K` be algebraically closed fields and `g : X ⟶ Y` a proper
morphism of `k₀`-schemes of finite type with `Y` quasi-projective, `Y_K = Y ×_{k₀} Spec K` and
`g_K : X_K = X ×_Y Y_K ⟶ Y_K` the base change. Normality, integrality and dimension of `X` and
`Y`; projectivity, surjectivity, being an isomorphism and smoothness of `g`; smoothness of `X`
and `Y`; relative ampleness of invertible sheaves; for normal varieties, birationality and
smallness; and, for `X` smooth, the simple normal crossing property of a closed subset, all hold
for `g` exactly when they hold for `g_K`.

Surjectivity, being an isomorphism and smoothness ascend by base change and descend along the
fpqc covering `Y_K ⟶ Y`. Birationality of a proper morphism to a normal variety is equivalent to
its generic fibre being the spectrum of the function field of the target, and the generic fibre
of `g_K` is a base change of that of `g`. The exceptional locus of `g_K` is the preimage of that
of `g`, both being complements of finite-fibre loci, and codimensions are compared through
`dim closure {x} + coheight x = dim X`. Simple normal crossings are tested on regular systems of
parameters, which ascend along the flat stalk maps of `X_K ⟶ X` (whose closed fibres are regular,
`κ(x) ⊗_{k₀} K` being regular) and descend along flat local homomorphisms.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_finiteEtaleCover_pointFibreChernClass_transport`: line bundles on very
  general fibres spread over finite étale covers, compatibly with parallel transport.
* `MMP.Fourfold.fibre_comparison`: for a proper morphism `f`, classes on the fibre `F_b(ℂ)`
  extend to tubes `f^an⁻¹(V)`, and classes vanishing on `F_b(ℂ)` vanish on a smaller tube.
* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_stalk_higherDirectImage_iso_of_taut`: for a continuous map whose fibre
  `p⁻¹(b)` is taut, `(R^q p_* ℚ)_b ≅ H^q(p⁻¹(b); ℚ)`, compatibly with germs and restrictions.
* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_stalk_higherDirectImage_iso`: hence, for `f` proper,
  `(R^q f^an_* ℚ)_b ≅ H^q(f^an⁻¹(b); ℚ)`, compatibly with germs and restrictions.
* `MMP.Fourfold.mapCoeff_rationalCohomologyMap`: the change of coefficients
  `H^n(-; ℤ) ⟶ H^n(-; ℚ)` commutes with pullbacks.
* `MMP.Fourfold.isEmbedding_analyticMap_fibre`: the realization of the scheme fibre `F_b` is
  imbedded onto `f^an⁻¹(b)`.
* `MMP.Fourfold.finiteDimensional_rationalCohomology_preimage_singleton`: for `f` projective,
  every `H^q(f^an⁻¹(b); ℚ)` is finite-dimensional.
* `MMP.Fourfold.t2Space_analyticSpace`, `MMP.Fourfold.hasOpenContractibleBasis_analyticSpace`,
  `MMP.Fourfold.isProperMap_analyticMap`: topology of complex realizations (locally
  contractible, Hausdorff for separated schemes, proper maps for proper morphisms), and
  `MMP.Fourfold.analyticMap_eq_mapFun` reading realizations on underlying spaces. Connectedness
  and local path connectedness (`MMP.Fourfold.connectedSpace_analyticSpace`,
  `MMP.Fourfold.locallyPathConnectedSpace_analyticSpace`) come from the imported module.
* `MMP.Fourfold.baseChange_iff_of_isAlgClosed`: the geometric properties used by a minimal
  model program are invariant under extension of an algebraically closed ground field.

## Implementation notes

* A class in `𝒲_t` is attached to a line bundle on `F_t` as for
  `MMP.Fourfold.IsPuncturedIndependent`: it is the germ of a class `α ∈ H²(π⁻¹(V); ℚ)`, on a
  neighbourhood `V` of `t` in `Y^an`, restricting to the first Chern class on `F_t`. By proper
  base change the restriction `𝒲_t ⟶ H²(F_t; ℚ)` is an isomorphism, so this is the source's
  identification.
* Parallel transport along `γ` carries `w ∈ 𝒲_t` to `v ∈ 𝒲_{t₁}` when some global section of
  the pullback `γ^* 𝒲` to `[0, 1]` has germ `w` at `0` and germ `v` at `1`. As `𝒲` is a local
  system, `γ^* 𝒲` is constant on `[0, 1]`, so such a section is determined by either germ.
* The sheet `F_{t₁} × {t'}` is `F_{t₁}`, mapped into `𝓕 ×_{T°} T'` by the morphism whose
  components are the inclusion `F_{t₁} ⟶ 𝓕` and `F_{t₁} ⟶ Spec ℂ ⟶ T'` through `t'`.
* The closed points of `T°` are its complex points; `Ω` is a countable set of proper closed
  subsets of the scheme `T°`, and `t ∉ Ω` means that the image of `Spec ℂ` under `t` lies in
  none of them.
* The finite étale cover is built by commutative algebra on affine charts: a closed point of the
  generic fibre is a maximal ideal of `B ⊗_R K`, `K = Frac R`; the quotient of `B` by its
  contraction is generically finite and generically étale over `R`, since `K` has
  characteristic zero, and a single localization `R_d` makes it finite étale. The source's
  normalization step is not needed.
* The fibre comparison for proper maps is proved by deforming tubes onto fibres, not by proper
  base change.
* In the field-extension theorem, the divisor of the simple normal crossing clause enters only
  through its support, so it is stated for an arbitrary subset `D ⊆ X`.

## References

* [Kollár–Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KM98]
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

